# Generated cinematic media (experiment/cinematic-media-*).
#
# INTERMEDIATE / CACHE — always ignored. Reproducible from media-src/ by the
# cinematic-media-converter and scroll-video-optimizer skills:
#   node ../ai-workflows/skills/cinematic-media-converter/scripts/extract-frames.mjs #     media-src/astronaut-hero-source.mp4 --outdir public/media/generated #     --name astronaut-hero[-97] --widths 1440,1080,720 [--every 2]
# Candidate video encodes are regenerated per docs/cinematic-hero-benchmark-2.md.
public/media/generated/**/w*/
public/media/generated/**/matte-preview/
public/media/generated/**/*.mp4
#
# FINAL RUNTIME — manifest.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the runtime
# contract the hero reads (frame count, tiers, naming), it is small, and it
# makes a regeneration with a different frame count reviewable.
#
# NOTE: if a frame-sequence hero is ever adopted for production, its runtime
# tier must stop being ignored — either committed like the MP4s in public/media,
# or generated by a documented build step. See docs/cinematic-hero-benchmark-2.md.
